TYPE=u32
GROUP=max
DOC=THE WHOLE-FLEET CEILING — how many dwarves may exist at once, counting lane runes.
DEFAULT<<'SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF'
    # THE WHOLE-FLEET CEILING — how many dwarves may exist at once, counting lane runes.
    # SPIRA_MAX_DWARVES is the task pool and a lane draws outside it, so the two of them
    # together are the box's real ceiling (pool + one per lane) and neither one alone is the
    # answer to "how many dwarves run at once". That is correct while the constraint is cores.
    # It is wrong while the constraint is a single shared account, which every dwarf draws on
    # and which the operator's own sessions draw on too.
    #
    # Declared empty, there is no ceiling. An upgraded host keeps what its config declares;
    # only a fresh install takes the registered default below.
    # Registered default (sp-kuwp6s, per Ryan 2026-10-07): A small single-box install: two dwarves at once across every persona and lane.
    : "${SPIRA_MAX_LIVE_DWARVES:=2}"
SPIRA_CONF_DEFAULT_EOF
